WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.230
- So you love Loretta Lynn?

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.220
Did you love her growing up?

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.233
- I love Loretta Lynn.

00:00:03.233 --> 00:00:04.800
- Me too.
- I really did.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.180
And I loved her growing up.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.690
And I grew up on country music,
traditional country music.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.430
Like, 'Three Chords And The Truth',

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.020
tin plated steel guitar kind of country.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.568
- Yes, that's my favorite.

00:00:14.568 --> 00:00:15.510
- And, me too.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.240
- And so I lived in
Nashville a couple of times.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.130
And, as a matter of fact,

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.240
I think we might have talked about this,

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.580
you guys will find this surprising.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.240
At one time, when I was 15
and hanging out in Nashville,

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.890
hanging out in bars, which
I shouldn't have been doing.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.620
But I was already like 6'
4", 220 with a mustache.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:32.580
I had a dream,

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.268
that my dream was I was
gonna be a country singer.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.325
- Oh, we had this talk.

00:00:36.325 --> 00:00:37.158
- Yeah.
- Yup.

00:00:37.158 --> 00:00:37.991
- And that was my dream.

00:00:37.991 --> 00:00:40.260
So what I used to do is, and
I had no money at that time.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.600
And I used to, that's where
all the country bars are at,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.860
and they're all like
dive bars, as you know.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.150
- Yeah, love.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.911
- And I would kind of like
walk the streets and be like,

00:00:47.911 --> 00:00:49.945
♪ I kicked the habit ♪

00:00:49.945 --> 00:00:51.262
♪ Smoking back something ♪

00:00:51.262 --> 00:00:52.514
(audience gasping)
- Hoping that someone.

00:00:52.514 --> 00:00:53.347
- Someone would be like, oh hark!

00:00:53.347 --> 00:00:55.980
- Someone would be like,
oh, what do you do?

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.120
You should come and sing.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.980
But then, it didn't happen for me.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.360
But I love Loretta.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.193
I love country.

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:02.026
And thank you for singing that with me.

00:01:02.026 --> 00:01:02.859
- Oh my God!

00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:03.962
I was so excited.

00:01:03.962 --> 00:01:04.795
(audience cheering)

00:01:04.795 --> 00:01:06.930
We literally like ran upstairs yesterday

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.130
and I was like, we gotta make this happen!

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:08.963
I love this song.

00:01:08.963 --> 00:01:09.796
I love her.

00:01:09.796 --> 00:01:10.770
There were so many songs
you could pick from.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.030
But speaking of country music.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.220
So I hear you recently went
back to the trailer park,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.630
that you used to live in,
like when you were a teenager.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.530
Was that, is it?

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.180
I kind of like going
back to my beginnings,

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.830
cause it's like it keeps it like fresh,

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.410
that reminder of man, I had
a big dream and it worked.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.243
You know?

00:01:23.243 --> 00:01:24.175
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:24.175 --> 00:01:26.070
- I, that was, it was real special for me.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:26.903
So two things.

00:01:26.903 --> 00:01:29.670
I, when I was 15, we were.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.560
Well we were evicted off
the island in Hawaii.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.970
We couldn't pay rent, so we were evicted.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:36.090
I got sent to Nashville
to live with my dad.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:38.160
Plans change, as they do.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.210
And I was then sent to live
with a guy who I didn't know

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.850
in a little motel room in Nashville.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.430
- That doesn't sound shady.
- No, it sucked.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.456
- Yeah.

00:01:48.456 --> 00:01:50.490
- But, you gotta do what you gotta do.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:51.856
What you're told to do, at least, at 15.

00:01:51.856 --> 00:01:52.689
- Yeah.

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:54.630
- So his name was Bruno, Downtown Bruno.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:58.170
Then, when I broke into pro wrestling,

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.960
before I got to the WWE,
I had to hit the road.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.580
Like I'm sure with you too as well,

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.610
where before that I wrestled
in a small promotion

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.230
where we were wrestling at flea markets,

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.670
and used car dealerships.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.503
You do what you gotta do.

00:02:09.503 --> 00:02:10.800
- My first time I ever
sang professionally was

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:11.683
at a wrestling match.

00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:13.710
It was the 'National Anthem'.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:14.543
- Oh, wow, see, so.

00:02:14.543 --> 00:02:15.660
- I had no idea what I was walking into,

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.860
and I wore a really fancy black dress.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.390
And it was like, this was wrong.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.500
I shouldn't have done this.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.333
- This was wrong.

00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:21.166
But the voice was right.

00:02:21.166 --> 00:02:21.999
- It was fine.
(laughing)

00:02:21.999 --> 00:02:23.940
I was very nervous, but it was low key.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:24.850
Not like WWE, it was like,

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.070
yeah, yeah.
- No, no, no, yes.

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.410
I mean, we would again,
flea markets and state fairs

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.460
is where I started.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.880
So then I went back and I didn't again,

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.370
I didn't have a place to live
cause I didn't have any money.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:38.370
And this guy, Bruno, put me in his place

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:39.900
and he had a little trailer.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.460
So, I recently went back after
all these years with Bruno,

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:45.840
and I went back to this trailer.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.680
This trailer park, actually
in walls, Mississippi.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.513
- Yeah.

00:02:50.513 --> 00:02:54.150
- And it was a really moving
moment cause it's like

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.910
all that stuff comes back to
you where it was struggle,

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.280
and it was uncertainty,
and what's gonna happen,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.113
and is this my life?

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.470
- Do you think that
that drives you though?

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.740
I feel like it drove me
to like kind of break out

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:05.573
and do something bigger.

00:03:05.573 --> 00:03:06.947
I knew that I was capable of.
- Yes.

00:03:06.947 --> 00:03:09.270
- I feel like that
struggle kind of helped.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:10.103
- Yes, Kelly.

00:03:10.103 --> 00:03:10.936
A hundred percent.

00:03:10.936 --> 00:03:14.040
And I, like you, I'm
sure like a lot of us,

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.470
I keep that right here in
the forefront of my mind.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:17.872
- Amen.
- Like I don't forget that.

00:03:17.872 --> 00:03:19.080
- Yeah.
- And that drives me.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.550
Cause to me I'm just

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.383
- It makes you're appreciative.

00:03:21.383 --> 00:03:22.740
- Yeah, and so grateful.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.390
Because it can all go away like that.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.130
So stay grounded and stay humble.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:26.963
- Yeah.

00:03:26.963 --> 00:03:27.796
I'm glad you got that experience.

00:03:27.796 --> 00:03:28.629
(audience cheering)
That's cool.

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:29.462
- It was amazing.

00:03:29.462 --> 00:03:30.295
- Yeah.

00:03:30.295 --> 00:03:32.130
- By the way, that trailer,
that little trailer,

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.240
has not changed one bit.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.400
It's the exact same trailer.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.233
- Oh, wow!

00:03:36.233 --> 00:03:37.066
- Small, kind of like

00:03:37.066 --> 00:03:38.220
- Like walking into your past.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.370
That's crazy.
- It was unbelievable, yeah.

